### ==============================================================================
### POLICYFLOW API EVALUATION & FAILURE-INJECTION DEMO
### Base URL: http://localhost:8000
### ==============================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000/api
@agentId = AGENT-17
@clientRequestId = AGT-2026-DEMO-01

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. INTAKE: Create a new policy request (HTTP 201 Created)
### Deterministic formula verification:
### DOB: 1998-04-10 (age 28 on trip_start 2026-11-10 -> age multiplier 1.00)
### Trip: 2026-11-10 to 2026-11-14 (inclusive 5 days)
### Plan: PLUS (₹20/day) | Dest: INTERNATIONAL (1.80) | Sum Insured: ₹300,000 (1.25)
### Expected Premium: 20 * 5 * 1.00 * 1.80 * 1.25 = ₹225.00
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name createPolicy
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_request_id": "{{clientRequestId}}",
  "agent_id": "{{agentId}}",
  "customer_name": "Sample Customer",
  "date_of_birth": "1998-04-10",
  "destination": "INTERNATIONAL",
  "trip_start": "2026-11-10",
  "trip_end": "2026-11-14",
  "plan_code": "PLUS",
  "sum_insured": 300000
}

### Capture policyId from response
@policyId = {{createPolicy.response.body.data.id}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. RELIABILITY CASE A: Duplicate Intake (HTTP 200 OK Idempotent Return)
### Submitting identical agent_id + client_request_id returns the existing record
### without recalculating premium or duplicating database rows.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_request_id": "{{clientRequestId}}",
  "agent_id": "{{agentId}}",
  "customer_name": "Sample Customer",
  "date_of_birth": "1998-04-10",
  "destination": "INTERNATIONAL",
  "trip_start": "2026-11-10",
  "trip_end": "2026-11-14",
  "plan_code": "PLUS",
  "sum_insured": 300000
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. VALIDATION REJECTION: Invalid travel dates (HTTP 422 Unprocessable Entity)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_request_id": "AGT-INVALID-01",
  "agent_id": "{{agentId}}",
  "customer_name": "Invalid Customer",
  "date_of_birth": "1998-04-10",
  "destination": "INTERNATIONAL",
  "trip_start": "2026-11-14",
  "trip_end": "2026-11-10",
  "plan_code": "PLUS",
  "sum_insured": 300000
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. RETRIEVE POLICY & AUDIT TRAIL: Query details by ID (HTTP 200 OK)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{policyId}}
Accept: application/json

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. ISSUANCE: Standard Happy Path (HTTP 200 OK -> ISSUED)
### External insurer issues policy with unique policy_number (POL-XXXXXXXX)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{policyId}}/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Mock-Scenario: SUCCESS

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. STATE MACHINE TERMINAL PROTECTION: Attempt to re-submit ISSUED policy
### Rejected with HTTP 409 Conflict. Cannot regress or mutate terminal state.
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{policyId}}/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Mock-Scenario: SUCCESS

### ==============================================================================
### STANDOUT FEATURE: FAILURE-INJECTION DEMO (TIMEOUT & RECONCILIATION - CASE B)
### ==============================================================================

### Step 7.1: Create fresh request for timeout demo
# @name createTimeoutPolicy
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_request_id": "AGT-2026-TIMEOUT-DEMO",
  "agent_id": "{{agentId}}",
  "customer_name": "Timeout Demo Customer",
  "date_of_birth": "1990-01-01",
  "destination": "DOMESTIC",
  "trip_start": "2026-12-01",
  "trip_end": "2026-12-05",
  "plan_code": "BASIC",
  "sum_insured": 100000
}

@timeoutPolicyId = {{createTimeoutPolicy.response.body.data.id}}

### Step 7.2: Trigger TIMEOUT_AFTER_ISSUE scenario
### Insurer issues policy internally, but connection times out (HTTP 504 Gateway Timeout).
### Policy status transitions to NEEDS_RECONCILIATION.
# @name submitTimeout
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{timeoutPolicyId}}/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Mock-Scenario: TIMEOUT_AFTER_ISSUE

@providerRef = {{submitTimeout.response.body.provider_reference}}

### Step 7.3: Prove the mock insurer already holds the policy internally
GET {{baseUrl}}/mock-insurer/policies/{{providerRef}}
Accept: application/json

### Step 7.4: Reconcile the request
### Directly solves the assignment failure mode: recovers the existing policy number
### without triggering duplicate issuance or second provider call (HTTP 200 OK -> ISSUED).
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{timeoutPolicyId}}/reconcile
Accept: application/json

### Step 7.5: Verify policy is now ISSUED with the recovered policy number
GET {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{timeoutPolicyId}}
Accept: application/json

### ==============================================================================
### 8. TEMPORARY FAILURE & CONTROLLED RETRY
### ==============================================================================

### Step 8.1: Create request for temporary failure demo
# @name createTempFailPolicy
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_request_id": "AGT-2026-TEMPFAIL",
  "agent_id": "{{agentId}}",
  "customer_name": "Retry Demo Customer",
  "date_of_birth": "1988-06-15",
  "destination": "DOMESTIC",
  "trip_start": "2026-12-10",
  "trip_end": "2026-12-15",
  "plan_code": "PLUS",
  "sum_insured": 300000
}

@tempFailPolicyId = {{createTempFailPolicy.response.body.data.id}}

### Step 8.2: Submit with TEMPORARY_FAILURE (HTTP 503 Service Unavailable -> FAILED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{tempFailPolicyId}}/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Mock-Scenario: TEMPORARY_FAILURE

### Step 8.3: Safe retry with SUCCESS (HTTP 200 OK -> ISSUED with original snapshot)
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{tempFailPolicyId}}/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Mock-Scenario: SUCCESS

### ==============================================================================
### 9. ASYNC ISSUANCE & DUPLICATE CALLBACK DEDUPLICATION
### ==============================================================================

### Step 9.1: Create async request
# @name createAsyncPolicy
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "client_request_id": "AGT-2026-ASYNC",
  "agent_id": "{{agentId}}",
  "customer_name": "Async Callback Customer",
  "date_of_birth": "1994-08-22",
  "destination": "DOMESTIC",
  "trip_start": "2026-11-20",
  "trip_end": "2026-11-25",
  "plan_code": "BASIC",
  "sum_insured": 100000
}

@asyncPolicyId = {{createAsyncPolicy.response.body.data.id}}

### Step 9.2: Submit with DELAYED_CALLBACK (HTTP 202 Accepted -> PENDING_CONFIRMATION)
# @name submitAsync
POST {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests/{{asyncPolicyId}}/submit
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json
X-Mock-Scenario: DELAYED_CALLBACK

@asyncProviderRef = {{submitAsync.response.body.data.provider_reference}}

### Step 9.3: First Callback Delivery (HTTP 200 OK -> PROCESSED, moves to ISSUED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mock-insurer/callback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": "EVT-MANUAL-CB-001",
  "provider_reference": "{{asyncProviderRef}}",
  "event_type": "POLICY_ISSUED",
  "policy_number": "POL-CALLBACK-7777"
}

### Step 9.4: Repeated Callback Delivery (HTTP 200 OK -> DUPLICATE_IGNORED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/mock-insurer/callback
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "event_id": "EVT-MANUAL-CB-001",
  "provider_reference": "{{asyncProviderRef}}",
  "event_type": "POLICY_ISSUED",
  "policy_number": "POL-CALLBACK-7777"
}

### ==============================================================================
### 10. OPERATIONS & MONITORING ENDPOINTS
### ==============================================================================

### Summary metrics and policies needing reconciliation (HTTP 200 OK)
GET {{baseUrl}}/operations/summary
Accept: application/json

### List policies with filtering and pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/policy-requests?status=ISSUED&per_page=10
Accept: application/json
